      "content": "thanks. can u finish that bit about the fees?\n\nalso, for the presentation, i need to explain why sometimes even with a \"well-organized\" passive fund, the returns don't perfectly match the index. there are these tiny, annoying discrepancies and small, unexpected leaks in value that happen during trading. is there a way to describe those little \"unseen\" disruptions or errors that seem to just sneak in and eat away at the total returns? i want to make sure the client understands how they can pile up unnoticed.",
